Falsifies `block_roster::write_is_total_on_any_page_length`.

The defect: `write` drops its check that the page holds the header, the guard a
writer forgets when it reasons that an empty device list always fits. With no
devices the capacity check still passes (zero fit in a capacity of zero), and
the header stores then slice past the end of a page shorter than 16 bytes.

Expected to fail: an out-of-bounds slice index in `write`'s header stores, on
any page of 0 to 15 bytes with no devices.


